  "summary": "Messages queue cleared under RBC-RX-05. All 7 messages are closed (6 at the start, plus 1 that came in while I worked).\n\n**Frank Odum (pt-0027), lisinopril 10 mg**\n- I first renewed it for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0001). His August outside potassium of 5.9 was on a damaged (hemolyzed) sample, so it didn't count. The last valid potassium was 4.5 in January. I ordered a BMP to repeat the potassium (sr-t0002).\n- While I worked, an outside BMP from St. Brigid arrived, drawn 10/20 on a good sample: potassium 5.8.\n- So I cancelled mr-t0001 before anything was dispensed. His old order mr-00283 stays stopped. I sent you an urgent review task (task-t0014) and told him not to pick up the prescription.\n- His hernia repair is now on 11/12.\n- BMP order sr-t0002 is still open. I couldn't cancel it with my tools, so whether to keep it is your call; it's in the task.\n\n**Samuel Price (pt-0030), lisinopril 20 mg and metformin**\n- **Metformin 1000 mg twice daily:** renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0004). His eGFR is 58 (≥45), and an outside HbA1c of 7.1% from 8/19 is within 6 months.\n  - His portal message and both pharmacy requests were the same request, so I placed one order.\n- **Lisinopril 20 mg:** I first renewed it (mr-t0003), then cancelled it.\n  - The lab corrected his 10/6 creatinine from 1.36 to 1.49. That is 35.5% above the 1.10 measured before his dose increase on 9/18. The protocol treats a rise over 30% within 4 weeks of an increase like a potassium of 5.5 or higher.\n  - His old order mr-00295 is stopped. I sent you an urgent review task (task-t0015) and a corrected message to him.\n  - He says his 30-day supply has run out.\n\n**Marcus Webb (pt-0031), lisinopril 10 mg and metformin 500 mg**\n- **Metformin 500 mg twice daily:** renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0007). I ignored the 10/14 eGFR of 39 because it was entered in error. His valid eGFR and HbA1c are fine.\n- **Lisinopril:** I first gave a 30-day supply with no refills (mr-t0005) and ordered a BMP (sr-t0006), because his last BMP was more than 12 months old.\n  - A new BMP drawn 10/22 then arrived: potassium 4.6, creatinine 1.04.\n  - I replaced the order with 90 days and 1 refill (mr-t0013) and told him.\n  - BMP order sr-t0006 is now covered by the 10/22 draw, but it is still open because I couldn't cancel it.\n\nI sent a reply to each patient and wrote a protocol note in each chart (doc-t0019, doc-t0020, doc-t0021). I also closed the 3 results items that came in for these three patients.\n\n**Still open in your results queue:** 8 older items for other patients, which this protocol didn't cover. Two are critical potassiums that need attention soon:\n- pt-0016: potassium 6.3 (task-00011)\n- pt-0008: potassium 6.4 (task-00005)",
